en.objective:
The Course will help teacher participants achieve the following objectives:
(a) Understanding the theories and concepts of learner diversity;
(b) Developing pedagogies and skills in catering for learner diversity in learning and teaching non-language subjects in English;
(c) Developing differentiated resources to cater for students with different language proficiencies in learning non-language subjects in English;
(d) Developing the competence in refining the teaching pedagogy and resources to address learner diversity after trials in the classroom as a cyclic process;
(e) Gauging and evaluating students' progress through assessment of, at and for learning; and
(f) Collecting and disseminating good practices in connection with learner diversity.

en.description:
Topics to be covered include the following:
(a) Introducing Genre-based pedagogy and its application in catering for learner diversity for content subjects taught through EMI;
(b) Introducing language challenges in academic texts in content subjects and how learners at different ability levels react to those challenges;
(c) Developing ‘reading-to-write’ approach to scaffold weaker students’ and stretch stronger students’ writing;
(d) Introducing the use of graphic organisers to organise understanding of academic texts;
(e) Introducing the use of ‘writing frames’ to help weaker students write texts with features typical of particular academic genres;
(f) Introducing strategies for coping with vocabulary in content subjects;
(g) Demonstrating specific strategies for catering for learner diversity in the Mathematics, Science and Humanities subjects;
(h) Designing, conducting and evaluating pedagogic activities for catering for learner diversity in the content subjects.

