en.objective:
This workshop offers teachers practical suggestions on how to bring drama into the mainstream English language classroom. It explores how to develop memorable and enjoyable learning experiences using process drama and readers’ theatre. The workshop promotes not only language learning but also how students’ cognitive growth, executive functioning, interpersonal skills and values are developed through drama activities.
This online workshop provides opportunities for teachers to:
explore the role of drama in developing students’ cognitive growth, executive functioning and interpersonal skills;
identify why drama improves students’ literacy and communication skills;
interpret the teacher’s role as a facilitator and reflective practitioner while using drama in the classroom; and
examine how drama can be integrated into the Hong Kong classroom through process drama and readers’ theatre.

