en.objective:
This workshop explores practical techniques for fostering creativity in young authors and poets, demonstrating how process writing can be used to teach poetry and help students create their own work.
This online workshop provides opportunities for teachers to:
examine the definition, features, and forms of creative writing;
understand the relationship between process writing and creative writing, and how process writing supports effective creative outcomes;
explore teaching techniques that support students' creative writing, including the use of strong models, a poet's tool kit, micro and macro revisions, and metacognition with an emphasis on effect;
examine three poetry forms and features — Diamante, Haiku, and Rap — as models for the teaching of poetry;
investigate how to combine a teaching technique with a poetry form to plan a poetry session, supported by a lesson plan template and sample; and
consider practical considerations for teaching creative writing in the classroom.

