en.objective:
The Programme will help each participant school achieve the following objectives:
(a) Understand language policy planning as well as reviewing the whole-school language policy, school-based MOI arrangements and measures for supporting students to learning through the English medium at a whole-school level;
(b) Cultivate teachers' curriculum leadership and enhance teachers’ capacity in reviewing and developing their school-based curriculum, designing and developing learning, teaching and assessment materials, and designing learning and teaching strategies to facilitate students’ effective learning of the Personal, Social & Humanities Education KLA in the English medium;
(c) Enhance the teaching pedagogy and skills of Personal, Social & Humanities teachers with the collaboration between the English language and Personal, Social & Humanities teachers within their own schools;
(d) Develop school-based curriculum and teaching strategies with differentiated instructions to cater for learner diversity in the Personal, Social & Humanities Education KLA in the English medium;
(e) Support teachers to develop the paradigm and skills required for continuous professional development to meet the changing needs of students which include, among others, equipping teachers with the knowledge and skills in conducting assessment for, as and of learning to feedback on teaching and learning;
(f) Strengthen the interface between the junior secondary and senior secondary school-based Personal, Social & Humanities curricula; and
(g) Refine pedagogy and materials after trials in the classroom as a cyclic process.

en.description:
Language across the Curriculum (LAC): From Theory to Sustainable Practice in the Secondary School classroom in Hong Kong schools. This is an informative, practical and skills based programme taking a ‘connected approach’ to LAC across the curriculum.
The programme connects:
(i) subject knowledge and its English Language patterns;
(ii) pedagogy with effective LAC delivery in the subject classroom;
(iii) connects formative assessment practices with effective subject MOI; and
(iv) new LAC knowledge with immediate and effective school based and classroom practice.
It has been specifically designed for PSHE KLA teachers and our aim is to develop teachers’ capacity to embed the best of LAC practice into their school's current educational reforms with specific reference to;
-Effective MOI for PSHE KLAs teachers
-Development of empowered and self-directed learners
-Formative assessment practices
-Pedagogies for enhanced student engagement
-Classroom language and classroom dialogues
-How to have co-agency with AI in developing resources
(1) Duration of Programme: October 2026 – July 2027;
(2) Total Contact Hours: A 30-hour Programme with 3 components:
(a) 3-hour training session at the Main Campus of The Hong Kong Polytechnic University in Hung Hom Kowloon;
(b) 24 hours based at each school for school-based support activities; and
(c) 3-hour dissemination session at the Main Campus of The Hong Kong Polytechnic University in Hung Hom Kowloon;
(3) Number of schools: 5-7 schools;
(4) No. of participants per school: 4-8 teachers per school;
(5) Participating teachers from each participating school: At least 1 Personal, Social & Humanities teacher and at least 1 English Language teacher.
(6) Course Coordinator: Dr Jane Lockwood
(7) Course Instructor: Mr Peter Woodhead

