en.objective:
The programme aims to enhance teachers’ knowledge and skills in the teaching of English in primary and secondary schools in Hong Kong. It places particular emphasis on recent pedagogical practices and practical ideas and strategies for English language teaching in the digital era that address the needs of contemporary English language classrooms and current curriculum developments in the local school sector. It also seeks to broaden teachers’ understanding of new possibilities for applying these practices to facilitate learning and teaching in the English classroom.
Upon completion of the programme, participants should be able to:
1. Review and reflect on the current practices of teaching English in schools in Hong Kong;
2. Develop an understanding of recent pedagogical strategies for English language teaching and learning, particularly those emerging from the digital era;
3. Explore practical ideas, resources, and classroom activities, including technology-enhanced approaches, to support students’ English language development; and
4. Apply appropriate teaching strategies to enhance learning, teaching, assessment, student engagement, and language development in English classrooms.

