en.background:
The optimised senior secondary History curriculum will be implemented in S4 in 2027-28 school year.
Curriculum Development Institute, EDB and Department of History, Hong Kong Baptist University co-organise a series of professional development programmes (including seminars and field trips) with the theme of 'Series on Supporting the Optimised Senior Secondary History Curriculum' starting from 2026-27 school year onwards, so as to support the implementation of the optimised senior secondary History curriculum.
This programme series includes knowledge-enrichment seminars on 'Topics in Modern and Contemporary World History'. The first six seminars are tentatively confirmed below:
Seminar 1: 'Module 1 The making of the modern world' (22/10/2026 PM);
Seminar 2: 'Module 2 War and Peace: The First World War (1)' (29/10/2026 PM);
Seminar 3: 'Module 2 War and Peace: The First World War (2)' (19/11/2026 PM);
Seminar 4: 'Module 2 War and Peace: The Second World War and the post-war international order (1)' (22/1/2027 PM);
Seminar 5: 'Module 2 War and Peace: The Second World War and the post-war international order (2)' (3/2/2027 PM);
Seminar 6: 'Module 2 War and Peace: The development of Asia, Africa and Latin America' (18/3/2027 PM)
Details for the above seminars and related field trip activities will be announced in due course.

