en.objective:
Upon completion of the workshops, participants will be able to:
• enhance their pedagogical content knowledge and theoretical understanding of teaching in a small class context;
• understand why and how to adopt a range of teaching strategies aligned with the six principles* to optimize learning in a small class context;
• enhance their capacity in applying self-regulated learning to facilitate learning and teaching in a small class environment.
*Note:
The six principles are：(1) setting clear learning objectives; (2) making good use of effective questioning techniques; (3) encouraging active pupil participation; (4) increasing cooperation between/among pupils by pair/group work; (5) using more informing feedback; (6) adopting the assessment for learning approach to enhance learning and teaching

