1. Assist teachers to understand the basic operating concepts of artificial intelligence (AI), including its underlying logic and limitations;
2. Equip teachers with practical prompting skills to enhance efficiency in lesson planning, instructional design, and school administration;
3. Develop the skills of using diverse AI platforms flexibly, while learning the way of verifying and refining AI-generated content for effective human-AI collaboration.

en.description:
1. Introduction to the basic operating logic of AI, including text processing, conversation context retention, and practical limitations;
2. Sharing of practical, universal prompting techniques and formulas to streamline daily lesson planning, instructional design, and school administration; and
3. Understanding the key features of different AI tools and mastering strategies to refine prompts and rectify inaccuracies in AI-generated content.

