en.objective:
The course will help teacher participants achieve the following objectives:
(a) Strengthening participants’ awareness in facilitating the language use by students in the whole-school approach to using the English medium;
(b) Enhancing participants’ knowledge and understanding of the language features that are specific to different non-language KLAs and the language requirements in the process of students’ learning (e.g. writing procedure, making hypothesis, reporting, describing, explaining, etc);
(c) Familiarising participants with vocabulary items or terms that need special attention in content subject areas (e.g. technical terms, figurative terms, words with multiple meanings, words easily confused with other words and acronyms, etc);
(d) Enhancing participants’ competence in reinforcing the language skills of students in respect of the academic English of different non-language KLAs to be expected for use by students;
(e) Developing pedagogies and skills in addressing learner diversity; and
(f) Developing strategies in promoting collaboration with non-language teachers across the curriculum.

