en.objective:
1. To enable school personnel to understand the current situation of cyberbullying in schools;
2. To equip school personnel with the skills for handling cyberbullying through case sharing;
3. To explore the roles of school personnel in preventing school bullying (including cyberbullying); and
4. To recognise participating schools.

The one-day workshop shall help participants, preferably those newly-joined teachers using English to teach the Technology Education, Arts Education and Physical Education (TAPE) Key Learning Areas (KLAs) subjects concerned, achieve the following objectives:
(a) Developing strategies and pedagogy for enhancing classroom communication by using subject-specific language in English;
(b) Understanding the concept and structure of academic English and its differences between the language of school and everyday language;
(c) Developing knowledge of the vocabulary items, terms and language features that are specific to the TAPE KLAs concerned, and the language requirements in assessing students’ learning; and
(d) Understanding, acquiring and deploying teaching strategies and classroom management techniques for learning and teaching the TAPE KLAs effectively in EMI, including but not limited to: presenting and explaining subject content clearly and systematically, eliciting students’ responses through questioning, giving students opportunities to demonstrate their learning in English, helping students with different language proficiencies and learning abilities in developing subject-specific English proficiency (e.g. speaking about the subject and writing on subject-specific assignments), and giving appropriate feedback to help students improve their learning.

en.description:
The course will include the following contents:
(a) Nature of the language of Technology Education, Arts Education and Physical Education KLAs and issues relating to learning and teaching of the non-language subjects concerned using English as the medium of instruction;
(b) Identifying genres in EMI classrooms: Semantics, semiotics, rhetorical structures, text knowledge in Technology Education, Arts Education, and Physical Education KLAs;
(c) Organisation of interactive activities and enhancement of communication skills in EMI classrooms;
(d) Drawing cross-curricular links and promoting Language across the curriculum;
(e) Strategies for designing pedagogic activities in EMI Technology Education, Arts Education, and Physical Education KLAs;
(f) Questioning and feedback-giving techniques that help students with different language proficiencies and learning abilities engage in EMI activities; and
(g) Designing effective formative and summative assessment tasks to address content and language objectives within the curriculum.

