en.objective:
To enhance teachers’ pedagogical knowledge and skills in teaching English in Hong Kong primary and secondary schools using literary and creative texts of different genres, with a focus on advancing students’ English proficiency while engaging the aesthetic, intellectual, cultural, and emotional dimensions of language learning in alignment with the latest English Language curriculum developments.
Upon completion of the programme, participants will be able to:
• Critically evaluate and reflect on current English language teaching practices in Hong Kong, particularly in relation to the use of literary and creative texts to support language learning;
• Demonstrate a clear understanding of how literary and creative works (e.g., stories, poems, drama, multimodal texts) can be systematically integrated into English teaching to enhance students’ language proficiency and engagement;
• Design and implement evidence-informed pedagogical strategies and classroom activities that utilise literary and creative texts of different genres to support students’ language development; and
• Explore and apply approaches that foster students’ aesthetic appreciation, critical thinking, cultural awareness, and emotional engagement in English language learning.

